NOTE: this file describes an older goose-era topology (kaji-bench, kaji-server,
kajid, ui/desktop) that no longer matches this workspace — see AGENT-GUIDE.md.
The Electron desktop app (`ui/desktop`) has been removed; the desktop target is
Tauri v2 on ACP, not yet implemented. Kept for historical reference; do not
rely on it for the current crate map (use `crates/` directly).

This is a rust project with crates in the crates dir:
kaji: the main code for kaji, contains all the core logic
kaji-cli: the command line interface, use kaji crate
kaji-mcp: the mcp servers that ship with kaji. the developer sub system is of special interest

non trivial features should be implemented in the kaji crate and then be called from the kaji-cli crate for the cli.

tips:
- can look at unstaged changes for what is being worked on if starting
- always check rust compiles, cargo fmt etc and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings` (as well as run tests in files you are working on)
